{
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "ADP-S7-PILOT",
      "title": "pilot: omni-plc-sim S7 (s7-1500 profile) -> s7 adapter (PLC4X 0.9.1) -> file",
      "intent": "The S7 adapter's first case on an S7 server. PLC4X 0.9.1 connects with ControllerType unset (COTP CR/CC with SFC's default TSAPs, Setup Communication negotiated down to the s7-1500's PDU 960 and AmQ 3, SZL 0x0011 identification) and reads 53 channels in one Read Var PDU per poll: every static DB1 type, including the raw SINT/USINT forms SFC builds for LINT, ULINT, LWORD, WCHAR, DATE_AND_TIME, STRING and WSTRING; M, I and Q bits, words and reals; and the dynamic DB100 signals, in all three deployment modes. Static values must arrive exactly and dynamic values stay in range and change over 8 records; the simulator's request log proves the handshake, the single PDU and that no error reply or dropped frame occurred. If it fails: a wrong handshake byte hangs connect() (PLC4X has no timer) and fails the record gate; a decoding or IPC conversion regression shows as a missing channel (keySet) or a wrong value. It avoids every adapter defect of the S7 spec (section 8): D1 (negative LREAL: lreal and sine64 are left out and t is never negative), D2 (raw forms outside DBs: only simple types in M, I and Q), D3 and D4 (the simulator always answers the handshake and returns the SZL record 0x0001), D5 (ULINT at or above 2^53), D6 (negative TIME), D7 and D8 (DATE_AND_TIME and TIME_OF_DAY instead of the DT and TOD aliases; DTL is read as SINT[12]), D9 (non-ASCII text), D10 (DATE outside UTC: the harness sets TZ=UTC), D11 (no reload), D12 (no metric assertions), D13 (rack 0) and D14 (offsets below 65536); it reads no BOOL arrays.",
      "pins": [
